<title>HUNGARY: Hungary Aug net household savings rise HUF53.5bln.</title>
<headline>Hungary Aug net household savings rise HUF53.5bln.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Net household savings rose 53.5 billion forints in August to 2,205.5 billion, the National Bank of Hungary said on Thursday.</p>
<p>	(in billion forints)   Aug 96     July 96	 Aug 95</p>
<p> Forint savings		 2,087.9     2,040.7	1,628.2</p>
<p> Foreign currency		 469.5	 463.2	  390.3</p>
<p> Total savings		  2,401.2     2,343.3	1,900.2</p>
<p> Total loans			351.9	 354.6	  381.2</p>
<p> Net savings		    2,205.5     2,149.3	1,640.3 @</p>
<p>NOTE: Figures are not inflation adjusted. This year's figures are preliminary. The consumer price inflation was 22.9 percent year-on-year in August. Since July, savings of individual entrepreneurs and family businesses were added to the NBH's net household savings figures.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4040</p>
